#
# Conformance case: cognition/contested-assessments
# AC (ME12, design/LOGIC-COGNITION.md §The cognitive assessment is reified):
# an assessment is vantage-indexed like any other claim — a self-assessment and an
# observer's assessment of the same agent on the same dimension are two COEXISTING
# records, never reconciled into one verdict. This case carries two contested
# logic:CognitiveAssessment instances of one agent (ada) on one dimension
# (metacognition) attributed to two standpoints via gmeow:accordingTo, with
# DIFFERENT levels (self: strong, observer: emerging).
#
# A non-reconciling rule surfaces each assessment's evaluator (ex:assessmentHeldBy)
# so the materialized output shows BOTH assessments retained, each attributed to its
# own evaluator (ada vs mentor) — nothing collapses the two differing levels into a
# single verdict.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/cognition/contested-assessments/> .
@prefix rdf:   <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .

ex:ruleAssessmentHeldBy a logic:Rule ;
    logic:provenance ex:ruleAssessmentHeldBy ;
    logic:head [ rdf:subject "?assessment" ; rdf:predicate ex:assessmentHeldBy ; rdf:object "?evaluator" ] ;
    logic:body [ rdf:subject "?assessment" ; rdf:predicate logic:assessmentEvaluator ; rdf:object "?evaluator" ] .
